„­bible_version£KJV¤book§chapter¨sections•…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ`And Samson went down to Timnath, and saw a woman in Timnath of the daughters of the Philistines.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ§And he came up, and told his father and his mother, and said, I have seen a woman in Timnath of the daughters of the Philistines: now therefore get her for me to wife.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚThen his father and his mother said unto him, Is there never a woman among the daughters of thy brethren, or among all my people, that thou goest to take a wife of the uncircumcised Philistines? And Samson said unto his father, Get her for me; for she pleaseth me well.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ®But his father and his mother knew not that it was of the LORD, that he sought an occasion against the Philistines: for at that time the Philistines had dominion over Israel.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse	¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ•Then went Samson down, and his father and his mother, to Timnath, and came to the vineyards of Timnath: and, behold, a young lion roared against him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙºAnd the Spirit of the LORD came mightily upon him, and he rent him as he would have rent a kid, and he had nothing in his hand: but he told not his father or his mother what he had done.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙIAnd he went down, and talked with the woman; and she pleased Samson well.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙªAnd after a time he returned to take her, and he turned aside to see the carcase of the lion: and, behold, there was a swarm of bees and honey in the carcase of the lion.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÍAnd he took thereof in his hands, and went on eating, and came to his father and mother, and he gave them, and they did eat: but he told not them that he had taken the honey out of the carcase of the lion.¦layout ªlast_verse	…¤book§chapter«first_verse
