¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙgSo his father went down unto the woman: and Samson made there a feast; for so used the young men to do.¦layout ªlast_verse
„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ[And it came to pass, when they saw him, that they brought thirty companions to be with him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÛAnd Samson said unto them, I will now put forth a riddle unto you: if ye can certainly declare it me within the seven days of the feast, and find it out, then I will give you thirty sheets and thirty change of garments:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¥but if ye cannot declare it me, then shall ye give me thirty sheets and thirty change of garments. And they said unto him, Put forth thy riddle, that we may hear it.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines”‚¤text¶And he said unto them,¦layout ‚¤textÙ!Out of the eater came forth meat,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ+And out of the strong came forth sweetness.¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ4And they could not in three days expound the riddle.¦layout­mid_paragraphªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙğAnd it came to pass on the seventh day, that they said unto Samson's wife, Entice thy husband, that he may declare unto us the riddle, lest we burn thee and thy father's house with fire: have ye called us to take that we have? is it not so?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚAnd Samson's wife wept before him, and said, Thou dost but hate me, and lovest me not: thou hast put forth a riddle unto the children of my people, and hast not told it me. And he said unto her, Behold, I have not told it my father nor my mother, and shall I tell it thee?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÑAnd she wept before him the seven days, while their feast lasted: and it came to pass on the seventh day, that he told her, because she lay sore upon him: and she told the riddle to the children of her people.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines“‚¤textÙ§And the men of the city said unto him on the seventh day before the sun went down, What is sweeter than honey? And what is stronger than a lion? And he said unto them,¦layout ‚¤textÙ$If ye had not plowed with my heifer,¦layout§quote_1‚¤text¿Ye had not found out my riddle.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙıAnd the Spirit of the LORD came upon him, and he went down to Ashkelon, and slew thirty men of them, and took their spoil, and gave change of garments unto them which expounded the riddle. And his anger was kindled, and he went up to his father's house.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙMBut Samson's wife was given to his companion, whom he had used as his friend.¦layout ªlast_verse